{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.BorromeanVolume","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.BorromeanVolume","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolumeSqueeze","lean:module:QOU.Knot.CatalanValueBounds"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.volumeConjectureBorromean_proved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.volumeConjectureBorromean_proved","kind":"instance","line":947,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L947-L949","doc":"The proved instance — machine-checked (B1–B5), no sorry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjectureBorromean.limit_eq_vol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjectureBorromean.limit_eq_vol","kind":"theorem","line":942,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L942-L942","doc":"`(2π/N)·log ⟨𝓑₃⟩_N → Vol(𝓑₃) = 8·Cl₂(π/2) = 8G` as `N → ∞`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjectureBorromean.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjectureBorromean.mk","kind":"ctor","line":940,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L940-L940","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjectureBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjectureBorromean","kind":"class","line":935,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L935-L945","doc":"**The Borromean per-link volume-conjecture carrier**, mirroring\n`VolumeConjecture41`: the single content field is the limit identity for\nthe positive-sum carrier. Kept as a class for downstream API symmetry\nwith the 4₁ instance; the instance below is a genuine sorry-free proof\n(brick B5), not a citation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_log_borromeanKashaev_vol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_log_borromeanKashaev_vol","kind":"theorem","line":919,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L919-L933","doc":"**The Borromean volume-conjecture instance, machine-proved (B5).**\n`(2π/N)·log ⟨𝓑₃⟩_N → Vol_Borromean = 8·Cl₂(π/2) = 8G` — the Whitehead-\nchain case of the Kashaev volume conjecture (van der Veen in the\nliterature), proved here by the elementary Riemann-sum squeeze of bricks\nB1–B5 for the positive-sum carrier `borromeanKashaev` (see the file\nheader for the carrier's epistemic status). The `8G` nuclear binding\nscale and the `F_Bor` anchor ride on this limit. (bean qou-jor3) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_two_pi_log_borromeanKashaev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_two_pi_log_borromeanKashaev","kind":"theorem","line":676,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L676-L917","doc":"**Borromean brick B5 — the squeeze (sorry-free).** The scaled Borromean\nKashaev log tends to the Borromean hyperbolic volume:\n`(2π/N)·log ⟨𝓑₃⟩_N → 8·Cl₂(π/2) = 8G = Vol(𝓑₃)`. Upper envelope: the\nsum has at most `N` terms, each at most the B5a ceiling; lower envelope:\nthe single grid term at `l* = ⌊3N/4⌋` (the `x = 3/4` saddle), whose B3c\ndeviation target converges to the saddle value by continuity of\n`clausen`. (bean qou-jor3) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.psi_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.psi_le","kind":"theorem","line":569,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L569-L674","doc":"**Borromean brick B5a — the per-term ceiling (sorry-free).** For every\nsurviving `l`, the B3c deviation target is at most the continuum saddle\nvalue plus the vanishing slack:\n`Ψ(l) ≤ 4·Cl₂(π/2) + borromeanSlack N`. Three cases: `2l+1 = N` and\n`2l = N` land on endpoint `clausen` values absorbed by the slack; the\ngeneric `2l ≥ N+1` case is the B4 max plus one log-sine cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_borromeanSlack","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_borromeanSlack","kind":"theorem","line":503,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L503-L566","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanSlack_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanSlack_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":494,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L494-L501","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanSlack","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanSlack","kind":"def","line":486,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L486-L492","doc":"The Borromean grid-to-continuum slack: the vanishing corrections between\nthe B3c deviation target and the B4 continuum functional (endpoint\n`clausen` values near `π`, `2π`, `0`, plus one log-sine cell). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanFunctional_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanFunctional_le","kind":"theorem","line":388,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L388-L484","doc":"**Borromean brick B4 — the continuum max (sorry-free).** On `[π/2, π]`\nthe Borromean functional never exceeds its saddle value `4·Cl₂(π/2)`,\nattained at `a = 3π/4` (the `x = 3/4` Kashaev saddle): compactness gives\na maximiser; the boundary values vanish while the saddle value is\npositive (certified Catalan bounds), so the maximiser is interior and\ncritical; the critical equation `(2 sin a)² = 2 sin(2a−π)` forces\n`sin a + cos a = 0`, hence `cos 2a = 0` with `2a ∈ (π, 2π)`, hence\n`a = 3π/4`. (bean qou-jor3) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanFunctional_three_quarters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanFunctional_three_quarters","kind":"theorem","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L374-L386","doc":"The saddle value: `G(3π/4) = 4·Cl₂(π/2)` — B1 antisymmetry route. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanFunctional_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanFunctional_pi","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L369-L372","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanFunctional_pi_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanFunctional_pi_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L363-L367","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_borromeanFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_borromeanFunctional","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L339-L361","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.continuous_borromeanFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.continuous_borromeanFunctional","kind":"theorem","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L331-L337","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanFunctional","kind":"def","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L324-L329","doc":"The Borromean continuum functional\n`G(a) = −4·clausen(2a) + clausen(4a − 2π)` — the limit of the scaled\nterm-log `8F(a) − 2F(2a−π)` (the B3c target with the vanishing\n`F((N−1)π/N)` and the one-cell `F`-shift dropped). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_log_borromeanTerm_deviation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_log_borromeanTerm_deviation","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L287-L322","doc":"**Borromean brick B3c — the uniform deviation (sorry-free).** On the\nsurviving range with `N ≥ 4`, the scaled term-log deviates from its\nClausen-primitive continuum value by at most `12·E(N)`:\n`|(π/N)·log borromeanTerm(N,l) − (8F(lπ/N) − 2F((N−1)π/N) −\n2F((2l+1−N)π/N))| ≤ 12·masterErr N`, `F(x) = −clausen(2x)/2` —\none E5c-4 deviation per `S`-index (`8+2+2` copies of `E(N)`), the\n`2l+1−N = 0` edge exact (`S(0) = F(0) = 0`). (bean qou-jor3) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_borromeanTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_borromeanTerm","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L267-L285","doc":"**Borromean brick B3b — the term log identity (sorry-free, exact).**\n`log borromeanTerm(N,l) = 8·S(l) − 2·S(N−1) − 2·S(2l+1−N)` — combining\nthe E5a bridge (`log kashaevProd = 2·S`) cubed with the B3a window\nidentity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_borromeanDen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_borromeanDen","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L139-L265","doc":"**Borromean brick B3a — the window identity (sorry-free, exact).** On the\nsurviving range, the log-denominator is an exact combination of the E4/E5\nRiemann sums `S(k) = Σ_{j≤k} log(2 sin(jπ/N))`:\n`log D(N,l) = 2·(S(N−1) − S(l) + S(2l+1−N))` — the window `(l, 2l+1]∖{N}`\nsplits at `N` and the upper half mirrors down by `sin(x+π) = −sin x` with\n`Real.log` absorbing the sign. No new deviation machinery needed.\n(bean qou-jor3) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanTerm_le_borromeanKashaev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanTerm_le_borromeanKashaev","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L128-L137","doc":"Single-term floor: each surviving term bounds the sum below (the E1-style\nlower envelope hook for the B5 squeeze). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanKashaev_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanKashaev_pos","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L117-L126","doc":"**The Borromean Kashaev sum is positive for `N ≥ 2`** — `log` of it is\nwell-defined, the floor the B5 squeeze stands on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanTerm_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanTerm_pos","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L112-L115","doc":"Every surviving Borromean term is strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanDen_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanDen_pos","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L63-L110","doc":"Every denominator factor index is a non-multiple of `N` in `(0, 2N)`,\nso its sine is nonzero and the squared factor strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanKashaev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanKashaev","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L57-L61","doc":"The Borromean Kashaev invariant at the `N`-th root of unity, as the\npositive sum over the surviving range `2l+1 ≥ N` (see file header for\nprovenance and epistemic status). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanTerm","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L53-L55","doc":"One surviving term of the Borromean Kashaev sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanDen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.borromeanDen","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BorromeanVolume.lean#L46-L51","doc":"The Borromean denominator `D(N,l) = ∏_{j=l+1, j≠N}^{2l+1} (2 sin(πj/N))²`.\nNo mirror bookkeeping needed: squaring absorbs the sign of `sin` past\n`j = N`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}